story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids has come in under 90% of normal in August to September 36 times in 75 years since 1951, the most of any pair. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, April to May ran 134% of normal and August to September ran 68%. So far in 2026, February to March and March to April each came in at 51% on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1965, with grid 23319 at 54%.</p>"}
